{
 "_doc": "Proposed per-space `audio` blocks (see README section 'Schema'). In the real build each block lives inside 3d/spaces/<id>.json as \"audio\": {...}; here they are collected in one file so the demo does not touch shared files. Geometry refs: water:<id> (path/lip/footprint from the space's water list), anchored:<id> or anchored_asset:<asset> (all instances), hero, or explicit at/points/polygon. gain_db is the level at ref_m relative to the asset's baked loudness (loops are normalised to about -20 dBFS RMS). Round 2 (owner feedback): rushing and thunder are the bed wherever water moves; bubbles and trickles are sparse close-range accents (high rolloff, low gain); B1 corridors carry a distant through-rock rumble; big sources have leak_db paths; levels are sized by hydraulic power (flow x drop), see README section 11. Round 3: CC0 anchor recordings (anchor_thunder, anchor_river, anchor_surf; see CREDITS.md) layered under the procedural beds of the three big waters.",
